.TH CHARGEGUARD 1 "July 2026" "ChargeGuard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
chargeguard \- manage firmware-native Linux battery charging modes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chargeguard
.I COMMAND
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chargeguard
is the command-line client for ChargeGuard.
It discovers battery charging modes exposed by the Linux power_supply sysfs
interface and communicates with the ChargeGuard daemon over the system D-Bus.
.PP
ChargeGuard operates only on modes reported by the device firmware and kernel
driver.  It does not implement percentage charge thresholds or general power
management.  A mode being reported does not guarantee that a later write will
succeed; the driver, firmware, and authorization policy decide the result.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List all present battery devices discovered by ChargeGuard.
.TP
.BR current " [" DEVICE "]"
Show the current native charging mode for
.IR DEVICE .
When DEVICE is omitted, ChargeGuard selects the only discovered battery and
reports an error if no battery or multiple batteries are available.
.TP
.BR modes " [" DEVICE "]"
Show the firmware-reported modes offered for switching on
.IR DEVICE ,
including the raw tokens accepted by the backend.
Device selection when DEVICE is omitted is the same as for
.BR current .
.TP
.BR set " [--device " DEVICE "] " MODE
Request a change to the exact firmware-reported raw
.IR MODE .
When
.B --device
is omitted, ChargeGuard selects the only discovered battery.
The daemon reads the available modes before writing, rejects values not
reported by the device, writes through the native sysfs interface, and verifies
the result by reading it back.
This is the only mutating command and is subject to the
.B io.github.ChargeGuard1.set-native-mode
polkit action.
.TP
.BR doctor " [--json]"
Collect a local diagnostic snapshot containing backend version, kernel and
service information, discovered devices, relevant power_supply attributes, and
explicit collection failures.
With
.BR --json ,
write the structured snapshot as JSON.  Without it, write a human-readable
report.  Partial data is retained when individual sysfs reads fail.
.TP
.BR raw " [" DEVICE "]"
Show the raw power_supply observations used by ChargeGuard, optionally limited
to DEVICE.  Collection issues affecting the output are shown explicitly.
.SH DEVICE SELECTION
The optional DEVICE value is the power_supply device identifier, such as
.BR BAT0 .
For commands that accept an omitted device, automatic selection succeeds only
when exactly one present battery is discovered.  Pass DEVICE (or
.BR "--device DEVICE"
for
.BR set )
on multi-battery systems.
.SH SAFETY
Before changing a mode, inspect
.B chargeguard modes
and use the raw token it reports.  ChargeGuard does not translate a requested
mode into thresholds and does not write modes absent from the device's reported
list.  The daemon performs the privileged write; ordinary inspection commands
do not require the set-mode polkit authorization.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS AND PRIVACY
.B doctor
and
.B raw
read local sysfs and service state.  Their output can include local device
identifiers, model information, filesystem paths, and driver-provided values.
ChargeGuard does not transmit this information, but review diagnostic output
before sharing it.
.SH ERRORS
Errors are written to standard error in the stable form
.PP
.RS
.I code: message
.RE
.PP
where code is a machine-readable snake_case identifier and message is
human-readable context.  Examples of error conditions include an unsupported
device or interface, an ambiguous device selection, an invalid mode, denied
authorization, sysfs read or write failure, readback mismatch, unavailable
service, and an internal protocol or parsing failure.  Programs should use the
code rather than parse the message.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The requested command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Discovery, D-Bus communication, authorization, validation, diagnostics, or a
native interface operation failed.
.SH FILES AND INTERFACES
.TP
.I /sys/class/power_supply
Kernel power_supply devices and firmware-native charging-mode attributes.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dbus-1/system-services/io.github.ChargeGuard1.service
System D-Bus activation definition.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dbus-1/system.d/io.github.ChargeGuard1.conf
System bus policy.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/io.github.ChargeGuard1.policy
Authorization policy for changing a native mode.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/chargeguardd.service
The D-Bus-activated backend service.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
Available native interfaces and raw mode tokens are hardware-, firmware-, and
kernel-driver-specific.  Some systems expose no supported interface, and a
kernel or firmware change can alter the available modes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR polkit (8)
.PP
Project documentation: https://github.com/Ca11back/ChargeGuard
